<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.route.binds ~ a new slot opens the same key

`lares vault bind` opens the vessel key with a route the hand types, then binds a new slot (`passphrase=true`, the default, or `paper=true`) that opens the same key; `face=N` binds the slot into that face's own tree, leaving the node tree untouched. A paper sheet just read back joins the keep pair too. A credential rides a TTY alone: no flag, no environment variable and no pipe carries one, nothing echoes one, and it drops the instant the act returns.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ passphrase · paper-face

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`passphrase` params=`passphrase/true ~ bind a passphrase slot to the vessel key`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`paper-face` params=`face/2 paper/true ~ bind a paper slot into face h2's tree`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · passphrase · paper

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ bind into that face's own tree, by persona index`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`passphrase` params=`kind/switch needs/one-of:passphrase,paper ~ the new slot opens by passphrase (the default)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`paper` params=`kind/switch needs/one-of:passphrase,paper ~ the new slot opens by a paper sheet`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand key/route ~ a person types both routes at their own terminal; an AI seat names the command`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · face-not-named · error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[face.route.binds passphrase/true]] ~ passphrase=true and paper=true both stood, or face= names no handle index`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-named` params=`cure/[[face.route.binds face/2]] ~ no face of that index stands in the floor index`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`error` params=`~ the custody door's named refusals lead the line by class (OccupiedStoreRefusal, CustodyRefusal, TreeKeyRefusal, CensusRefusal, CustodyLockRefused, CustodyFoundingRefused, CredentialTtyRefusal, RotationSlotsRefused), exit 1`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ bound

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`bound` params=`exit/0 fields/[[slotId slots face]] ~ the new slot opens the key; slots counts those standing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

